('115.39.c.8.B',3,'An ad for a supplement says "doctors don''t want you to know this secret." This is an example of what?','["A public health warning", "Peer-reviewed evidence", "A marketing technique that may mislead", "Medical advice"]'::jsonb,2,'Be skeptical of exaggerated claims.','original'),
('115.39.c.8.B',3,'Celebrity endorsements in health ads are used to do what?','["Prove safety", "Replace research", "Provide data", "Persuade buyers by association with a popular person"]'::jsonb,3,'Endorsements are persuasion techniques.','original'),
('115.39.c.9.A',3,'Chronic conditions such as diabetes can have an economic impact on society by doing what?','["Increasing health care costs and lost work time", "Ending insurance", "Reducing costs", "Raising productivity"]'::jsonb,0,'Chronic illness is expensive.','original'),
('115.39.c.9.A',3,'A social impact of a chronic illness on a family can be what?','["Less stress", "Emotional stress and caregiving responsibilities", "No change", "Free care"]'::jsonb,1,'Illness affects families.','original'),
('115.39.c.9.B',3,'A plan for accessing community resources for a chronic condition could include what?','["Random ads", "No contact", "Support groups, a primary care provider and reliable online information", "Rumors"]'::jsonb,2,'Resources help manage conditions.','original'),
('115.39.c.9.B',3,'A digital resource is reliable for a health plan if it is from what?','["A sales page", "An anonymous poster", "A stranger", "A medical or government organization"]'::jsonb,3,'Credible sources matter.','original'),
('115.39.c.11.A',3,'If a student finds a firearm in an unsafe place, the safest response is to do what?','["Do not touch it, leave the area and tell an adult", "Pick it up", "Show friends", "Take it home"]'::jsonb,0,'Never handle found weapons.','original'),
('115.39.c.11.A',3,'A person who sees someone with a weapon at school should do what?','["Confront them", "Move to safety and report to staff or call 911", "Ignore it", "Film it"]'::jsonb,1,'Report and get safe.','original'),
('115.39.c.11.B',3,'A good home safety model for children includes what?','["Hiding smoke detectors", "Ignoring hazards", "Locking up medications, chemicals and weapons", "Leaving items out"]'::jsonb,2,'Safe storage prevents injury.','original'),
('115.39.c.11.B',3,'An educational safety model for a school might include what?','["No drills", "Secret plans", "Random rules", "Clear emergency drills and posted procedures"]'::jsonb,3,'Practice and clarity improve safety.','original'),
('115.39.c.12.A',3,'A consequence of posting an inappropriate image online is that it may do what?','["Stay online permanently and harm future opportunities", "Disappear immediately", "Have no effect", "Be private forever"]'::jsonb,0,'The digital footprint lasts.','original'),
('115.39.c.12.A',3,'Which is a consequence of cyberbullying for the victim?','["Higher confidence", "Anxiety, depression or fear of going to school", "Closer friendships", "Better grades"]'::jsonb,1,'Cyberbullying harms mental health.','original'),
('115.39.c.12.B',3,'Sharing someone''s private images without permission can be what?','["A harmless prank", "Always legal", "A crime with legal penalties", "A joke"]'::jsonb,2,'There are laws against it.','original'),
('115.39.c.12.B',3,'An ethical use of social media includes doing what?','["Impersonating others", "Posting anything", "Sharing rumors", "Respecting others'' privacy and getting permission before sharing"]'::jsonb,3,'Ethics means respect and honesty.','original'),
('115.39.c.13.A',3,'If a student sees a classmate being cyberbullied, the best response is to do what?','["Support the victim and report it", "Share the post", "Join in", "Laugh"]'::jsonb,0,'Intervention helps the victim.','original'),
('115.39.c.13.A',3,'A situation requiring adult intervention in bullying is one that involves what?','["A normal debate", "Threats, repeated harm or risk to safety", "A single polite disagreement", "A joke between friends"]'::jsonb,1,'Serious harm needs adults.','original'),
