('115.39.c.22.F',3,'A benefit of abstinence is that it allows a teen to focus on what?','["Personal goals, education and emotional health", "Risky behavior", "Only games", "Only gossip"]'::jsonb,0,'Abstinence supports future goals.','original'),
('115.39.c.22.F',3,'Choosing abstinence helps protect against what?','["Exercise", "Unintended pregnancy and STIs", "Friendships", "Good grades"]'::jsonb,1,'It eliminates the risk.','original'),
('115.39.c.22.G',3,'A teen creating strategies for abstinence might do what?','["Ignore friends", "Hide plans", "Plan activities, talk with parents and set clear limits", "Avoid advice"]'::jsonb,2,'Support makes plans stronger.','original'),
('115.39.c.22.G',3,'Support from parents and trusted adults helps a teen make healthy decisions because they do what?','["Give pressure", "Avoid talking", "Add stress", "Offer guidance, accountability and encouragement"]'::jsonb,3,'Support strengthens choices.','original'),
('115.39.c.22.H',3,'Under Texas law, sexual activity with a minor can be what?','["A crime, regardless of consent in many cases", "A game", "A civil matter only", "Always legal"]'::jsonb,0,'The law protects minors.','original'),
('115.39.c.22.H',3,'The age of consent in Texas is what?','["21", "17", "10", "13"]'::jsonb,1,'Texas sets the age of consent at 17.','original'),
('115.39.c.22.I',3,'Sexual harassment can be addressed by laws that do what?','["Reward it", "Allow it", "Prohibit unwanted sexual behavior and provide penalties", "Ignore it"]'::jsonb,2,'Laws protect victims.','original'),
('115.39.c.22.I',3,'Sexting images of a minor can lead to what?','["A warning only", "A prize", "Nothing", "Serious criminal charges"]'::jsonb,3,'Laws on child sexual images are strict.','original')
